//api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T16:38:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T16:38:37Z","body":"It looks like this has caused a regression where lightmaps aren't correctly applied to objects anymore","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3357225221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3357260292","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111054#issuecomment-3357260292","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111054","id":3357260292,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IG7oE","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T16:49:25Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T16:49:25Z","body":"@BlueCube3310 Which renderer?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3357260292/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402267616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111054#issuecomment-3402267616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111054","id":3402267616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Kynvg","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T14:51:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T14:51:46Z","body":"While I haven't gotten to measuring it, this PR is likely to have caused a performance regression due to the rearrangement of the values.\r\n\r\nThe reason behind material_id and shader_id being the MSB of the bitfield is that it allows the renderer to sort and group based on being able to avoid rebinding pipelines and materials as much as possible. By inverting their order on the keys, other less significant elements have now been prioritized and the possibilities of batching together compatible draw calls has been reduced.\r\n\r\nI'd make a PR myself to fix it, but I'd like to know OP's thoughts first into addressing this. The reason behind the original ordering is that:\r\n- Shaders can be often reused because BaseMaterial3D will assign the same shaders to materials if their configuration is similar, which means only textures must be rebound if groups of draw calls with the same.\r\n- Grouping materials avoids the need to rebind textures.\r\n- Grouping geometry avoids the need to rebind vertex and index buffers.\r\n\r\nThe other miscellaneous parameters having priority over these IDs are likely to cause inefficient ordering over the criteria I laid out above. If you'd prefer, I can address this ordering on a PR myself while keeping 'priority' as the MSB of the key.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402267616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402894968","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111054#issuecomment-3402894968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111054","id":3402894968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K1A54","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T17:20:28Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T17:20:28Z","body":"@DarioSamo I hadn't really thought of that. I was looking at the pr which changed the order and broke \"priority\" and assumed that the arrangement was just changed in order to make the bitmask simpler. I guess the fix would be reverting the bitmask changes from this pr + #111125, and then rearranging the \"*_id\" fields to be the msbs after \"priority\". If you want to make a pr to fix it, I say go ahead.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402894968/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]